  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 8104.02 Noncompliance",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 8104.02 Noncompliance. If inspected work in place is found to be not in compliance with applicable state building codes at the time of inspection, the inspector shall issue a written order to the permit holder to correct the non-compliant work. The corrected work shall be subject to a re-inspection to verify compliance, and the permit holder shall be subject to a re-inspection fee.\n\nSource. #12022, eff 10-26-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c8100.html"
}
